* SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
* VERSION: pt_pll_ring r12 STAGED (2026-11-20, ECO on r9v: ct_phbuf8m + ct_xc4 duty pairs, east strip +10.75 um; not published) / r9v (2026-11-12, r8ring RING ECO: r9d core layout kept as routed; old FT legs + VCF resistors removed; FT = header current-steered macro pt_pll_ring_ft (pll_ring_ft.spice, r9h scheme), hand layout; FU/FD/KP ports moved to the block bottom) / r9d (2026-11-11, RINGAREA: WT21 BAND bit, tail m8 + replica 6.67 (r9c); r9 2026-11-10) -- ports REF EN N4 N8 HOLD IBIAS PH0..PH7 LOCK FBCK REFO ATB_VCTRL N5 N10 KP0..KP2 FU0..FU3 FD0..FD3 BAND VDD VSS
* r9 (IX-1, PD9, AC3-W9; 2026-11-10): (1) ring cell ct_ring9 (interleaved layout, 2x ring devices): the extracted
*   ct_ring8 lost 42 % of its speed to cell wiring; r9 runs on the pt_pll_vreg output (VDD = ring supply, ~0.9 x rail)
*   and covers 393-834 MHz in ONE band with VCTRL 0.87..2.02 V (ff/22/3.015 .. ss/32/2.71 V; ring cell extracted).
*   (2) fast-tune units are tail/header copies (gate VCF / VPBF) so ppm/vote tracks the ring current (see below).
*   Low rates (IX-4) need no ring change: full-rate phase mapping with the ring at 2 x the bit rate (OSR 2).
* r8 (AC3-W7, AC3-W8): (1) N = 10 (N10: feedback VCO -> ct_div5 -> /2 = /10) and N = 5 (N5: REF/2 into the PFD with
*   the same /10 feedback, as N4 does with /8) for HDMI/DVI x10 (720p full rate, 1080p half rate).  Priority
*   N5/N10 > N4/N8.  The /5 counter is held in reset unless EN & (N5|N10).  Pump 10 uA in /10 modes.
* (2) CDR fast-tune (proportional) port: per vote leg k two gate-switched current legs on the ring tail
*   (VT) with 1/12-size copies on the header replica (VPB), so both rails move: leg on when FUk=1 and leg on
*   when FDk=0 -> FU only: +1 unit, FD only: -1 unit, neither/both: 0 (vs the idle level, a static offset
*   the integral path absorbs).  Unit = KP code (0..7, cdr.config kp bits) x one switched long-channel
*   conductance.  FUk/FDk come straight from the capture PD (one ring cycle each).  KP=0: path off.
* pt_pll_ring: wired-side PLL with the compact 8-phase ring (P3/P4 first cut).
* Shared loop pieces from pll.spice (PFD, charge pump, filter, lock detector);
* VCO = ct_ring8 (4-stage pseudo-differential ring, O0..O7 at 45 deg) with an
* NMOS tail on VT (gate VCTRL) and a PMOS header on VH; feedback = four
* ct_tspc2 TSPC /2 stages; N = 16 (N4=N8=0), 8 (N8=1) or 4 (N4=1, host_follow
* from the 125/156.25 MHz H2D_CLK).  N=4 is realised as REF/2 (TSPC) into the
* PFD with feedback /8, so the PFD never runs above ~80 MHz (an extracted
* PFD at 125-156 MHz did not hold lock).  This is the single PLL design for every loop (P3-2).  PH0..PH7 are the eight
* ring phases at the VCO rate (wired_rx phase-interpolator interface).
* EN=0: REF gated, PFD reset, filter discharged, header and tail off, phase
* outputs and TSPC stages clamped, LOCK=0.
* SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
* Shared transistor-level cells for the timing family (GF180MCU gf180mcuD,
* 3.3 V nfet_03v3/pfet_03v3 and ppolyf_u_1k only).  Every block .spice
* includes this file; layout, LVS and simulation read the same text.
* Convention: all cells take VDD VSS as their last two ports.

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- inverters
.subckt pt_t_inv1 A Y VDD VSS
XP Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XN Y A VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_t_inv2 A Y VDD VSS
XP Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XN Y A VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_t_inv4 A Y VDD VSS
XP Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.28u
XN Y A VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_t_inv8 A Y VDD VSS
XP Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.28u m=2
XN Y A VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.28u
.ends

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- gates
.subckt pt_t_nand2 A B Y VDD VSS
XPA Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XPB Y B VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XNA Y A X VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XNB X B VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
.ends
* Faster 2x NAND for GHz select gating.
.subckt pt_t_nand2x A B Y VDD VSS
XPA Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XPB Y B VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XNA Y A X VSS nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XNB X B VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_t_nand3 A B C Y VDD VSS
XPA Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XPB Y B VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XPC Y C VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XNA Y A X1 VSS nfet_03v3 w=3u l=0.28u
XNB X1 B X2 VSS nfet_03v3 w=3u l=0.28u
XNC X2 C VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=3u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_t_nand3x A B C Y VDD VSS
XPA Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XPB Y B VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XPC Y C VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XNA Y A X1 VSS nfet_03v3 w=6u l=0.28u
XNB X1 B X2 VSS nfet_03v3 w=6u l=0.28u
XNC X2 C VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=6u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_t_nor2 A B Y VDD VSS
XPA X A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XPB Y B X VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XNA Y A VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
XNB Y B VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_t_nor2x A B Y VDD VSS
XPA X A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.28u
XPB Y B X VDD pfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.28u
XNA Y A VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XNB Y B VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
.ends
* AND2 / OR2 composites
.subckt pt_t_and2 A B Y VDD VSS
X0 A B N VDD VSS pt_t_nand2
X1 N Y VDD VSS pt_t_inv1
.ends

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- latch / dividers
* Clocked (C2MOS) inverter: drives Y = !A while CKN=1 and CKP=0.
.subckt pt_t_cinv A Y CKN CKP VDD VSS
XP1 X A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XP2 Y CKP X VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XN2 Y CKN Z VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XN1 Z A VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
.ends
* Pseudo-differential C2MOS latch with cross-coupled keeper (strong enough to
* reject the common-mode state P=N that weak keepers allowed), so the
* state is static at any clock rate.  Transparent while EN=1, ENB=0.
* Non-inverting: OP follows DP.
.subckt pt_t_latd DP DN OP ON EN ENB VDD VSS
X0 DP ON EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinv
X1 DN OP EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinv
XKP1 ON OP VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN1 ON OP VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
XKP2 OP ON VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN2 OP ON VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
.ends
* Same latch with reset: RST=1 forces OP=0 / ON=1.  Used only as the slave
* (opaque while the clock pair is stopped at CKP=0), so reset never fights
* a transparent latch in the stopped state.
.subckt pt_t_latdr DP DN OP ON EN ENB RST VDD VSS
X0 DP ON EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinv
X1 DN OP EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinv
XKP1 ON OP VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN1 ON OP VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
XKP2 OP ON VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN2 OP ON VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
XR OP RST VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
.ends
* Master-side reset variant: RST=1 forces ON=0 / OP=1, which is exactly the
* value a transparent master copies from a reset slave, so it never fights.
.subckt pt_t_latdm DP DN OP ON EN ENB RST VDD VSS
X0 DP ON EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinv
X1 DN OP EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinv
XKP1 ON OP VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN1 ON OP VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
XKP2 OP ON VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN2 OP ON VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
XR ON RST VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
.ends
* Divide-by-two with quadrature outputs.  Clock pair CKP/CKN (complementary).
* RST is effective while the clock pair is stopped (CKP=0, CKN=1).
* Slave (I) changes on CKP rising, master (Q) on CKP falling: Q leads I by a
* quarter output period.  Output pairs are complementary by construction.
.subckt pt_t_div2 CKP CKN RST IP IN QP QN VDD VSS
XM IN IP QP QN CKN CKP RST VDD VSS pt_t_latdm
XS QP QN IP IN CKP CKN RST VDD VSS pt_t_latdr
.ends
* Edge-triggered pseudo-differential D flip-flop (rising CKP).
.subckt pt_t_dffd DP DN CKP CKN RST QP QN VDD VSS
XM DP DN MP MN CKN CKP VDD VSS pt_t_latd
XS MP MN QP QN CKP CKN RST VDD VSS pt_t_latdr
.ends
* Divide-by-five: 3-bit shift register with D0 = NOR(Q1,Q2); 40 % duty.
* Self-starting from every state.
.subckt pt_t_div5 CKP CKN RST OP ON VDD VSS
X0 D0P D0N CKP CKN RST OP ON VDD VSS pt_t_dffd
X1 OP ON CKP CKN RST Q1P Q1N VDD VSS pt_t_dffd
X2 Q1P Q1N CKP CKN RST Q2P Q2N VDD VSS pt_t_dffd
XNOR Q1P Q2P D0P VDD VSS pt_t_nor2
XNAND Q1N Q2N D0N VDD VSS pt_t_nand2
.ends

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- clock selection
* Y = (S0 & A) | (S1 & B) for pseudo-differential pairs; with S0=S1=0 the
* output is stopped at P=0, N=1.  S0/S1 must be one-hot or both 0; changing
* the selection is specified only through the stopped state (both 0).
.subckt pt_t_sel2 AP AN BP BN S0 S1 YP YN VDD VSS
XSN S0 S1 SN VDD VSS pt_t_nor2
XSB SN SNB VDD VSS pt_t_inv1
XA0 AP S0 NA0 VDD VSS pt_t_nand2x
XB0 BP S1 NB0 VDD VSS pt_t_nand2x
XO0 NA0 NB0 VDD YP VDD VSS pt_t_nand3x
XA1 AN S0 NA1 VDD VSS pt_t_nand2x
XB1 BN S1 NB1 VDD VSS pt_t_nand2x
XO1 NA1 NB1 SNB YN VDD VSS pt_t_nand3x
.ends
* OR-combine two stopped-or-running pairs (at most one running):
* YP = AP | BP, YN = AN & BN.  Same gate depth on both legs.
.subckt pt_t_comb2 AP AN BP BN YP YN VDD VSS
XIA AP APB VDD VSS pt_t_inv2
XIB BP BPB VDD VSS pt_t_inv2
XOP APB BPB YP VDD VSS pt_t_nand2x
XON AN BN YNB VDD VSS pt_t_nand2x
XIN YNB YN VDD VSS pt_t_inv2
.ends
* 2:1 multiplexer (single-ended): Y = S ? B : A.  AOI22 + inverter.
.subckt pt_t_mux2 A B S SB Y VDD VSS
XPA X1 A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XPSB X1 SB VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XPB YB B X1 VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XPS YB S X1 VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XNA YB A X2 VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XNSB X2 SB VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XNB YB B X3 VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XNS X3 S VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XI YB Y VDD VSS pt_t_inv2
.ends
* Faster first-stage divider: 2x C2MOS strength (for VCO-rate inputs).
.subckt pt_t_cinvf A Y CKN CKP VDD VSS
XP1 X A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.28u
XP2 Y CKP X VDD pfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.28u
XN2 Y CKN Z VSS nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
XN1 Z A VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_t_latdf DP DN OP ON EN ENB VDD VSS
X0 DP ON EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinvf
X1 DN OP EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinvf
XKP1 ON OP VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN1 ON OP VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
XKP2 OP ON VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN2 OP ON VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_t_latdfm DP DN OP ON EN ENB RST VDD VSS
X0 DP ON EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinvf
X1 DN OP EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinvf
XKP1 ON OP VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN1 ON OP VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
XKP2 OP ON VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN2 OP ON VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
XR ON RST VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_t_latdfr DP DN OP ON EN ENB RST VDD VSS
X0 DP ON EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinvf
X1 DN OP EN ENB VDD VSS pt_t_cinvf
XKP1 ON OP VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN1 ON OP VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
XKP2 OP ON VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.5u l=0.28u
XKN2 OP ON VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
XR OP RST VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_t_div2f CKP CKN RST IP IN QP QN VDD VSS
XM IN IP QP QN CKN CKP RST VDD VSS pt_t_latdfm
XS QP QN IP IN CKP CKN RST VDD VSS pt_t_latdfr
.ends
* Single-ended clock to complementary pair (CKN one inverter, CKP two).
.subckt pt_t_s2d A CKP CKN VDD VSS
X0 A AB VDD VSS pt_t_inv2
X1 AB CKP VDD VSS pt_t_inv4
X2 A CKN VDD VSS pt_t_inv4
.ends
* Single-ended one-hot select: Y = (A & S0) | (B & S1); 0 when stopped.
.subckt pt_t_sel2s A B S0 S1 Y VDD VSS
XA A S0 NA VDD VSS pt_t_nand2
XB B S1 NB VDD VSS pt_t_nand2
XO NA NB Y VDD VSS pt_t_nand2
.ends
* Y = A | B
.subckt pt_t_or2 A B Y VDD VSS
X0 A B N VDD VSS pt_t_nor2
X1 N Y VDD VSS pt_t_inv1
.ends
* 4-way single-ended one-hot select
.subckt pt_t_sel4s A B C D S0 S1 S2 S3 Y VDD VSS
X0 A B S0 S1 Y0 VDD VSS pt_t_sel2s
X1 C D S2 S3 Y1 VDD VSS pt_t_sel2s
X2 Y0 Y1 Y VDD VSS pt_t_or2
.ends
* SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
* Loop-piece library for pt_pll_ring (included by pll_ring.spice):
*   pt_pfd -- static NAND-DFF phase-frequency detector with RESET_N input.
* Not a block on its own (no layout or evidence of its own).

* ---- PFD ----
.subckt pt_pfd_inv A Y VDD VSS
XP Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XN Y A VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=1u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_pfd_nand2 A B Y VDD VSS
XP0 Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XP1 Y B VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XN0 Y A N VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XN1 N B VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_pfd_nand3 A B C Y VDD VSS
XP0 Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XP1 Y B VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XP2 Y C VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
XN0 Y A N1 VSS nfet_03v3 w=3u l=0.28u
XN1 N1 B N2 VSS nfet_03v3 w=3u l=0.28u
XN2 N2 C VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=3u l=0.28u
.ends
.subckt pt_pfd_and2 A B Y VDD VSS
XN A B N VDD VSS pt_pfd_nand2
XI N Y VDD VSS pt_pfd_inv
.ends
.subckt pt_pfd_dff D CLK RN Q QB VDD VSS
XDB D DB VDD VSS pt_pfd_inv
XCB CLK CB VDD VSS pt_pfd_inv
XMS D CB RN MS VDD VSS pt_pfd_nand3
XMR0 DB CB MR0 VDD VSS pt_pfd_nand2
XMR MR0 RN MR VDD VSS pt_pfd_and2
XMQ MS MQB MQ VDD VSS pt_pfd_nand2
XMQB MR MQ MQB VDD VSS pt_pfd_nand2
XSS MQ CLK RN SS VDD VSS pt_pfd_nand3
XSR0 MQB CLK SR0 VDD VSS pt_pfd_nand2
XSR SR0 RN SR VDD VSS pt_pfd_and2
XQ SS QB Q VDD VSS pt_pfd_nand2
XQB SR Q QB VDD VSS pt_pfd_nand2
.ends
.subckt pt_pfd REF FB RESET_N UP DN VDD VSS
XU VDD REF RN UP UPB VDD VSS pt_pfd_dff
XD VDD FB RN DN DNB VDD VSS pt_pfd_dff
XRESET UP DN BOTH_N VDD VSS pt_pfd_nand2
XRN RESET_N BOTH_N RN VDD VSS pt_pfd_and2
.ends
* pt_pll_ring_ft: CDR ring fast-tune array (r7ring r9v), header-side current steering, see pll_ring.spice
.subckt pt_pll_ring_ft VH VPBF KP0 KP1 KP2 FU0 FU1 FU2 FU3 FD0 FD1 FD2 FD3 EN IBIAS VDD VSS
* r9h FT legs (r7ring, 2026-11-11): HEADER-SIDE CURRENT STEERING.  r9c/r9d switched the SOURCE node of each
* long-channel tail/header copy; while a leg was off that node (tens of fF of Cgs) recharged from VT/VH and was dumped
* at the next turn-on, so every vote transition moved charge into the ring: +4360..+4830 ppm for net-zero FU/FD
* alternation (r9c ext / r9d sch), data-dependent.  r9h: the ring is header-limited (r7ring: tail-only copies give
* ~1/3 of the gain), so only header copies remain.  Each binary PMOS copy (gate VPBF, source at VDD through its static
* KP switch) conducts ALWAYS and stays saturated; its drain is steered by a complementary PMOS switch pair into VH
* (vote active) or into VHD, held at V(VH) by a follower (replica feed-forward + push-pull transconductor, below).
* The steered drain only moves by |VH - VHD| (mV) on a saturated device, and each switch returns its channel charge
* within one on/off cycle (half-size dummies on VH cancel the VH-side share).  U: into VH when FUk=1.  D: into VH when FDk=0 (idle offset absorbed by the integral path).
XKPI0 KP0 KPB0 VDD VSS pt_t_inv1
XKPI1 KP1 KPB1 VDD VSS pt_t_inv1
XKPI2 KP2 KPB2 VDD VSS pt_t_inv1
* VHD follower: (1) feed-forward: a replica of the nominal dump current (4 binary copy sets = one per leg, same
* KP switches) into an NMOS diode, mirrored 1:1 as a sink on VHD, so at idle the follower carries no current;
* (2) a push-pull transconductor for the vote-dependent rest: NMOS pair (VHD | VH), PMOS diode loads, x2 mirrors:
* sink 2*I(VHD side) via an NMOS mirror, source 2*I(VH side); net 0 at balance.  VHD is the only high-impedance
* node (dominant pole, 4 pF decap).  Tail = 4 x the IBIAS mirror (10 uA each).  EN=0: no bias, VHD shorted to VH (so it starts at V(VH) when the ring starts; no slewing from a rail).
XHFT HFT IBIAS VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=4u l=2u m=4
XHF1 HFA VHD HFT VSS nfet_03v3 w=8u l=1u
XHF2 HFB VH HFT VSS nfet_03v3 w=8u l=1u
XHFA HFA HFA VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.5u
XHFB HFB HFB VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.5u
XHFAM HFN HFA VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.5u m=2
XHFND HFN HFN VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.5u m=2
XHFNS VHD HFN VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.5u m=2
XHFBM VHD HFB VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.5u m=2
XHFC VSS VHD VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=10u l=10u m=8
XRDD RDN RDN VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.5u
XRDS VHD RDN VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.5u
XHR0 RDN VPBF ZR0 VDD pfet_03v3 w=0.44u l=1.75u m=4
XHR0k ZR0 KPB0 VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=0.44u l=0.28u m=4
XHR1 RDN VPBF ZR1 VDD pfet_03v3 w=0.88u l=1.75u m=4
XHR1k ZR1 KPB1 VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=0.88u l=0.28u m=4
XHR2 RDN VPBF ZR2 VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.76u l=1.75u m=4
XHR2k ZR2 KPB2 VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=1.76u l=0.28u m=4
XHFZ VHD EN VH VDD pfet_03v3 w=2u l=0.28u
